schema: "0.4"
id: phosphor-19-error-and-recovery-notices
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns (a CLI learning tool) — Error & Recovery Notices, the inline notice pattern. Showcases the ONE sanctioned hue break.
# Theme tenets: monochrome amber CRT, single glowing hue on warm near-black, fixed-width mono as the primary UI face, radius 0, box-drawing chrome, zero elevation.
# Palette: amber #ffb000, warm near-black #140c00, dim amber #c88a00, bright amber #ffd050; error = red-shifted phosphor #ff5a3c — the ONLY non-amber on any screen, and only here.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    monochrome amber-CRT terminal — ONE warm amber hue on a warm near-black void,
    fixed-width monospace as the primary UI face for everything, radius 0, box-drawing
    chrome, zero elevation. The screen is otherwise monochrome amber; a SINGLE red-shifted
    "error" tone is the one and only sanctioned break, used once, so a hard failure is
    unmistakable in the amber field. Terse, machine, all-business register. This is a real
    terminal, never a web page.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a single amber-on-black TERMINAL WINDOW where an inline
    ERROR & RECOVERY notice has interrupted a running session for a command-line knowledge
    base. Fill the frame with ONE terminal window and a thin top title bar; there is NO web
    browser chrome, no tabs, no address bar, no rounded website panels.

    The whole surface is one warm AMBER hue on a warm near-black background EXCEPT for a
    single red-shifted "error" tone used exactly once (see ERROR BANNER). Hierarchy is
    carried by BRIGHTNESS and glyphs, never by hue. Fixed-width monospaced type everywhere.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (top to bottom):

    DIMMED SESSION BEHIND: the top third shows the ordinary session it interrupted —
    a prompt line and a few answer rows — rendered in DIM, faded amber so it clearly
    recedes behind the notices.

    ERROR BANNER (the focal point): a box-drawn banner whose rule and leading glyph are in
    the single RED-SHIFTED error tone (a hot orange-red, distinct from every amber on
    screen), led by a bright "✗" glyph — "✗ quarantined: kb/rust/async.md — unparseable
    YAML at line 14". This is the ONLY non-amber element anywhere in the image. Two dim
    amber body rows beneath explain it in plain terms and reassure that the session did not
    crash and no data was lost.

    WARNING NOTICE (amber, for contrast): a second stacked box-drawn banner, this one fully
    AMBER (not red), led by a "! " glyph — "! backend unreachable: Claude Code auth expired
    — run: robot-learns auth login". This proves warning and error are told apart by glyph
    and tone, not color alone.

    GUIDED RESOLUTION: a box-drawn pane titled "┤ RECOVERY ├" with numbered monospaced
    steps in amber — "1  restored from atomic pre-write copy", "2  re-run validate when
    ready" — and a row of bracketed mono buttons "[ view file ]  [ retry ]  [ dismiss ]"
    where the primary "[ retry ]" is reverse-video (amber fill, near-black text).

    BOTTOM STATUS RULE: a persistent reverse-video status bar across the full width with
    keybind hints "↵ resolve   esc dismiss   ^Q quit".

    PALETTE & TYPE: monochrome warm amber on warm near-black, with exactly ONE red-shifted
    error tone appearing a single time on the error banner — no green, no blue, no rainbow,
    and no second use of red. Status is shown by glyphs (✗ ! i) and brightness. Fixed-width
    terminal font throughout, no proportional or sans typeface anywhere.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero rounded corners — every banner and pane is a sharp rectangle
    bounded by thin box-drawing rules; the notices are flat over a slightly dimmed backdrop
    with NO drop shadow. No gradients, glow bloom, scanlines, or screen curvature. Flat
    light on a dark void.

    MOOD: calm even in failure — a machine that caught the problem, protected the data, and
    is telling you exactly what to do; one amber field with a single unmistakable red break.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, web browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, rounded website cards, syntax-highlighting rainbow, green terminal text, multiple red elements, CRT scanlines, screen glow bloom, screen curvature"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Reads as an inline error/recovery interruption: a dimmed session behind, a red-shifted ✗ error banner (quarantined file), an amber ! warning banner for contrast, a box-drawn RECOVERY pane with numbered steps and bracketed buttons, and a bottom keybind status rule"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Monochrome amber on warm near-black with EXACTLY ONE red-shifted error tone used once; fixed-width mono for ALL text; radius 0; box-drawing banners not shadowed cards; status by glyph+tone not hue"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "The error banner is the clear focal point against the dimmed session; warning vs error legible by glyph; plausible real-CLI notice"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts, no CRT filter kitsch"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "web browser chrome or a marketing web page instead of a terminal window"
    - "green/blue/rainbow color, or red used on more than the single error banner"

tags: [phosphor, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
